---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Construction Quantity Reference | SteelCalc" description="Planning reference for concrete, masonry, plaster, flooring, and excavation quantity calculations used by SteelCalc.">
  <div class="page">
    <header><a href="/" class="brand">Steel<span>Calc</span></a><nav><a href="/calculators">Calculators</a><a class="active" href="/guides">Guides</a><a href="/tools">Tools</a></nav></header>
    <main><div class="eyebrow">CONSTRUCTION REFERENCE</div><h1>Quantity-estimating notes for <em>site work.</em></h1><p class="intro">These are planning references used to make calculator assumptions visible. They are not substitutes for project specifications, mix designs, or site measurements.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>SteelCalc approach</th><th>Planning note</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Concrete dry volume</td><td>Entered dry-volume factor</td><td>Common estimating practice varies; use the factor required by the project.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Concrete cement mass</td><td>Entered bag weight × estimated bags</td><td>Cement bulk density is an estimating assumption and can vary.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Masonry units</td><td>Wall volume ÷ unit module volume</td><td>Module includes mortar joint; openings and cutting are not automatically deducted.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Masonry mortar</td><td>Wall volume − solid unit volume</td><td>Actual mortar depends on bond, joint thickness, workmanship, and unit geometry.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plaster</td><td>Area × thickness</td><td>Thickness variation and surface preparation can materially change consumption.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Floor tiles</td><td>Floor area ÷ tile area + wastage</td><td>Pattern, cuts, breakage, and future replacement influence wastage.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Earthwork swell</td><td>In-situ volume × (1 + swell %)</td><td>Soil behavior depends on material, moisture, excavation method, and handling.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
:global(body){margin:0;background:#f6f7f8;color:#17212b;font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui}.page{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px 70px}header{height:78px;border-bottom:1px solid #e1e6e9;display:flex;align-items:center}.brand{font-size:18px;font-weight:850;text-decoration:none;color:#17212b;margin-right:auto}.brand span{font-weight:450;color:#6c7780}nav{display:flex;gap:24px}nav a{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#68747d;text-decoration:none}nav a.active,nav a:hover{color:#17212b}main{padding-top:55px}.eyebrow{font-size:7px;letter-spacing:1.8px;font-weight:850;color:#8b959d}h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,64px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-3.4px;margin:16px 0}h1 em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;color:#d9932f}.intro{max-width:760px;font-size:10px;line-height:1.8;color:#66747d}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;margin-top:32px}table{width:100%;min-width:720px;border-collapse:collapse;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e0e5e8}th,td{text-align:left;padding:13px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #edf0f2;font-size:9px;line-height:1.65}th{font-size:7px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#87929a;background:#fafbfb}td:first-child{font-weight:800;color:#38454d}
</style>